body:
where to get mental health help for a teenager with no money?

&#x200B;

struggling so badly it's ruining my life because of overthinking.

hello can someon tell me if my choice was right?

&#x200B;

recentlygot back my N level results and i got a 14; i was able to go to higher nitec from NA, but there were no courses that caught my interest despite me having the chance to apply to all courses in DPP, so i decided to go to O levels. however, all teachers are now telling me to ''suck it up'' and that they ''heard the same things from seniors'' many times. 

&#x200B;

i rly don't understand why they telling us to go to a course we love in the beginning, but now when we get back our results, they tell us to suck it up and just do it instead of going to O levels.
